# Convex codegen owns these, and it formats them itself.
#
# `npx convex dev` runs prettier over its own output with NO config resolution
# — `prettier.format(contents, { parser, pluginSearchDirs: false })` in
# `convex/dist/esm/cli/lib/codegen.js:613` — so a generated file always comes
# out in prettier's DEFAULTS: double quotes, semicolons, unquoted keys. This
# repository's own config is the opposite on two of those three (`semi: false`,
# `singleQuote: true`).
#
# So `pnpm format` rewrote all 40 000 lines of each `api.d.ts` and the next
# codegen run rewrote them back, forever, and neither diff meant anything. The
# committed file must be what codegen writes — `convex-api-manifest.test.ts`
# reads it as the source of truth for which modules exist, and a file the
# formatter and the generator disagree about is one nobody can regenerate
# cleanly.
apps/*/convex/_generated
